# 6. Quick Reference

### Configure CLI

```bash
aws configure
```

### Verify AWS identity

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

### Check EC2 CloudTrail activity

```bash
aws cloudtrail lookup-events \
  --lookup-attributes AttributeKey=ResourceName,AttributeValue=<INSTANCE_ID> \
  --region <REGION_NAME> \
  --max-results 50 \
  --query 'Events[].{Time:EventTime,Event:EventName,User:Username}' \
  --output table
```

### Example Region

```text
ap-south-1
```

### Example Instance ID

```text
i-0123456789abcdef0
```

---

## Summary

Using **AWS CLI + CloudTrail**, we can check the infrastructure/API activity associated with an EC2 instance and identify **what action happened, when it happened, and which user/role performed it**.

For example:

```text
EC2 Instance
     ↓
CloudTrail
     ↓
Start / Stop / Reboot / Modify / Attach / Detach
     ↓
Time + User/Role
```
